MingTTS is a Swift and Metal port of the inference path of Ming-3.0-tts-0.5B
by inclusionAI:

- Code: https://github.com/inclusionAI/Ming-3.0-tts
- Model: https://huggingface.co/inclusionAI/Ming-3.0-tts-0.5B

This repository does not include the model weights, the tokenizer files or
the CAM++ speaker encoder (campplus.onnx). Download them from the Hugging
Face repository above. inclusionAI publishes them under its own license
(MIT at the time of writing); that license, not the Apache License, governs
the weights.

Parts of MingTTS follow the upstream Python code closely: the prompt layout,
the text frontend (normalization rules and fragment splitting), the task
modes, the sampling loop and the network definitions. The built-in voice
list in Sources/MingTTS/Text/MingVoiceCatalog.swift is generated from the
upstream cookbook, and the test fixtures in Tests/MingTTSTests/Fixtures hold
outputs of the upstream frontend and the Hugging Face tokenizer. The upstream
code carries this notice:

